A||||3||HotFieroGT||Grounding problem||||8||
Z||000000||HotFieroGT||12-26-1999||10:40 PM||||I have what I think is a ground problem, these are my symptoms.  The gas gauge works okay until about 1/4 of a tank then it swings above full, my temp gauge will climb all the way up then drop again over and over.  The ampmeter runs around 16 -17 volts (too high) and the oil pressure guage fluctuates.  Is there a common ground for all of the instruments?||||reg||8
Z||000001||862M4inCA||12-27-1999||03:19 AM||||Sounds to me like a loose/dirty ground connection.  I've checked my manual for the wiring schematic, and have found that there appears to be three separate ground wires coming from the instrument cluster itself.  It gave a couple numbers and one letter each wire having either the number or letter. Not sure if this is an index on the plug, but the wires are labeled K, 4, and 11. Might try checking with a test light to see that they've all got good connections. Hope this helps some.||||reg||1
Z||000002||HotFieroGT||12-29-1999||11:40 PM||||Thanks for the info, I am going to look for those grounds this weekend.||||reg||1
Z||000003||87GTBro||12-30-1999||02:31 AM||||I had grounding problems on my 86 GT.<BR>While my symptoms were quite different from yours, I will share what I found.<P>First, my symptoms were: When the car was idling, all lights pulsated with the engine.  Then if I was to turn on the headlights or the radio or the fan or the blinkers all the gauges on the instrument cluster would dance around and try to throw a party.<P>Last night, I broke up the party.  Unnoticed before, was the main braided ground wire that is supposed to stretch from the engine block to the decklid mounting bolt.  I saw that it was connected to the frame at the bolt and didn't pay attention to where the other end led to.  <BR>Needless to say, last night I found it wasn't connected to the engine block at all and I eleviated the problem.  Now everything is fine. (Although the battery did die on me... maybe that's why it was disconnected?)||||reg||1
